\subsection{Exact reduced spectral evaluation}
\label{sec:adaptation-reduced-mse-validation}
The reduction is checked using periodograms of the eight vessel-CG heave
records and the exact reconstruction cost
\begin{equation}
J_{\rm wave}(\omega_R)=\frac{1}{2\pi}\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}
\frac{1+4x^2}{1+x^6}S_\eta^{(2)}(\omega)\,d\omega,
\qquad x=\omega/\omega_R.
\label{eq:adapt-exact-wave-cost}
\end{equation}
Minimizing $3q_{\rm eff}/(2\omega_R^3)+J_{\rm wave}$ removes the high-frequency
approximation. For $\kappa_\star=F(\rho)$,
$\rho=q_{\rm eff}/(\widehat\sigma_{a,B}^2\tau)$ and
$s=\partial\log\kappa_\star/\partial\log\rho$, the local exponents are
\begin{equation}
p_a=6s,\qquad p_\tau=5/2+3s.
\label{eq:adapt-exponents-from-s}
\end{equation}
Table~\ref{tab:adapt-exact-mse-exponents} reports the numerical minima using
five-draw operating points. These are conditional, record-wise spectral
diagnostics, not independently fitted complete-filter optima.
